#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287647 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3913b813-19e1-5838-a7ce-25c5f75b98b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{15}{11},y=\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287649} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7fbde2-1a21-5fb1-8d83-65e0637b0829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-15,y=-10,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287650} {:answer/id #uuid "d49ea752-b50e-5647-ba94-f4bf5951285c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287651} {:answer/id #uuid "42da5cbf-1dcc-5f8e-aff0-1ee1c79574da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-30,y=-20,z=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287652} {:answer/id #uuid "5fdb890a-69a1-5c8a-b553-5afded12115b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=15,y=10,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d49ea752-b50e-5647-ba94-f4bf5951285c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287651} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed131fa2-13cf-592a-be0c-f93fee5f0963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e436b484-45cd-5959-9069-2880512ec233" :question/math-academy-id "q-10074" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z=-1-x \\\\ 4y=-5z \\\\ x+6z-3=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z=-1 \\\\ 4y+5z=0 \\\\ x+6z=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(24)-2(-5)+3(0-4) \\\\  & =24+10-12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 12 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}24 & 5 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{15}{11} \\\\ -\\frac{10}{11} \\\\ \\frac{8}{11}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287654 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40398599-c736-5231-83f6-dd91cf084a44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287656} {:answer/id #uuid "040386b6-5143-5e39-a9e4-c69c7af3cada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287657} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b433aa-17d2-5e91-a08f-3477affa21f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287658} {:answer/id #uuid "b996bbe6-77e2-52b4-a15a-6bcb715fd96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287659} {:answer/id #uuid "9330039e-54ee-52a6-9da7-c7c1b7494f8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40398599-c736-5231-83f6-dd91cf084a44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287656} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e58b42b-ea48-5337-bb06-7cf540036ffb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "528b601b-5416-5158-83e1-ea8ffb44a5a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-104536" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-2z=2+2y \\\\ 2y+4z=2x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-2y-2z=2 \\\\ -2x+2y+4z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-(8-4)+(4-4) \\\\  & =-4+0 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-4}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=2+1+0=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287661 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8f212da-c62b-5b55-8dfe-f1bd1c478789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,y=-11,z=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287663} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2060ec-2e80-5939-93e4-13de7ea9dbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11,y=-6,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287664} {:answer/id #uuid "acfb8a8b-781e-5d0f-b596-bb531721e814" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6,y=-3,z=-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287665} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf8785b-6265-5ef0-83d0-7ea910f09768" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11,y=6,z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287666} {:answer/id #uuid "f4274771-6965-5e28-85ca-7aed5b6b1f78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-11,y=6,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd2060ec-2e80-5939-93e4-13de7ea9dbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11,y=-6,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287664} :answer-field/id #uuid "789a32d6-dcb0-5fd8-b255-8b4bfb37e483" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf9ff59f-8ec8-569a-88c2-1ac3dd73e105" :question/math-academy-id "q-104541" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+z+x=2 \\\\ -3z+y=3 \\\\ 2x+y=4-4z\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=2 \\\\ y-3z=3 \\\\ 2x+y+4z=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4+3)-(0+6)+(0-2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1\\text{ }\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=11,y=-6,z=-3.$"}]}
